.policy "ruff-n817-camelcase-imported-as-acronym" revision 2
.description "Avoid aliasing a CamelCase import to an acronym of its capital letters; the alias reads like a constant and hides what the name is."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*"

// Ruff N817 (pep8-naming): a CamelCase name imported under the acronym of its capitals. Names are read as Ruff's
// parser reads them, NFKC-normalised, dotted names without their spacing. Exempt when the name or the alias matches
// `pep8-naming.ignore-names`, and when the alias is the import convention for the module: Ruff's default
// flake8-import-conventions aliases have one such entry, `xml.etree.ElementTree as ET` (absolute imports only; a
// relative `from ..xml.etree import ElementTree as ET` is reported).
//   from mod import CamelCase as CC          ← N817
//   import xml.etree.ElementTree as ET       not reported
//   from xml . etree import ElementTree as ET   not reported: the module is "xml.etree"
#include "python/python-20.rerail"

.violation N817(at: node, x: symbol, a: symbol) code "N817"
    "Import `{x}` under its own name, or a descriptive CamelCase alias, instead of the acronym `{a}`, and update its uses; keep the alias if your project's convention requires it."
    suppress ruff "N817"
N817(i, x, a) :- ruff_alias_import(i, x, a), ruff_camel(x), ruff_cased_upper(a), ruff_acronym(x, a),
    !ruff_import_full(i, "xml.etree.ElementTree"), !ruff_ignored(x), !ruff_ignored(a).
